  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying probable outcomes (with probability > 1/n) and comparing the average number of such outcomes. In this case, Lottery B has one probable outcome (100% > 50%), while Lottery A has none (both outcomes at 50%, not greater than 0.5). Thus, the reason would prefer B. However, the verbal report does not mention any reference to the threshold of 1/n, nor does it discuss probable outcomes or their count. Instead, it expresses a preference for a smaller loss, which is a different cognitive process. The individual’s justification (preference for smaller loss) does not match the rule of the decision reason (counting probable outcomes based on probability threshold). Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
